{
    "article_summary": "This article describes a transition metal-free, visible-light-driven photocatalytic synthesis of tetra-substituted furans from 1,3-diketones. The reaction is promoted by carbon dioxide (CO2), which acts as a catalytic promoter by incorporating into the enolic OH position to facilitate C-O bond cleavage and rearrangement of a cyclopropane intermediate. The method allows for the construction of two regioisomeric furan scaffolds under mild conditions using 4CzIPN as a photocatalyst.",
